        "original_id": "b9954e24-8aa8-5f5a-b52a-b9f5b5f824cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincent Knesevich de Szent-Helena, Meinhard II (Duke of Carinthia), Joseph Bach\n- Places: the county once ruled by Meinhard II with his brother, the crowned land associated with Joseph Bach\n- Topics: historical rule, military occupation, Austrian crown lands\n\nFacts:\n- Meinhard II, Duke of Carinthia, once ruled a county together with his brother.\n- In 1805, Vincent Knesevich de Szent-Helena had troops march into that county.\n- In 1867, Joseph Bach preached in the area identified as a crown land associated with that county.",
